<!--
    GH-468 (msvcstackguard follow-up): a 64-byte stack buffer terminated by an
    explicit zero prints one element short, with the terminator as a separate
    char.
    Witness: canary_check from the reporter's ab_od.exe (MSVC /Od /GS /Zi),
    the real 183 bytes at 0x140001160:

        int canary_check(const char *in) {
            char buf[64]; int acc = 0;
            strncpy(buf, in, sizeof(buf) - 1);
            buf[sizeof(buf) - 1] = 0;
            for (int i = 0; buf[i]; i++) acc += (unsigned char)buf[i];
            return acc;
        }

    buf is [rsp+0x30, rsp+0x70) against the /GS cookie at rsp+0x70.  The
    terminator is `mov rax,[rsp+0x28]` (= 1*0x3f) then
    `mov byte ptr [rsp+rax*1+0x30],0` at 0x1400011bf; heritage folds the
    constant index into a direct one-byte store at rsp+0x6f (stack - 0x19),
    and the scan loop's index is unbounded, so loadguardrange locks no range
    and the open hint for buf keeps the gatherOpen index floor of 3.
    RangeHint::attempt_join then rejects the store (63 > 3) and restructure
    ends buf at stack - 0x19.
    Stage: P6 stack-frame layout, option nulterminator on|off.  The zero is
    never read directly (only the loop's indexed LOAD can reach it), so with
    the option on the open range continues over it: `uint1 v [64]` and the
    store renders as the indexed `v[0x3f] = 0`.  The option off pins the old
    shape: `uint1 v [63]` beside a separate `char v; // stack - 0x19`.
    strncpy carries the libc prototype the loader gives the real binary;
    __report_rangecheckfailure and __security_check_cookie are shortened to
    their fast-fail shapes, and the cookie global is 0x140074040.
    read_back is a hand-assembled neighbour that stores the same zero at
    rsp+0x6f, passes buf to fill(), and then returns the byte READ BACK:

        sub  rsp,0x88
        mov  byte [rsp+0x6f],0
        lea  rcx,[rsp+0x30]
        call fill
        movsx eax,byte [rsp+0x6f]
        add  rsp,0x88
        ret

    The read makes the byte a variable of its own, so both passes keep
    `char v [63]` plus the separate char.
    Assertion counts span all four passes.
-->
